# BuildKit honors this `<Dockerfile>.dockerignore` (used by `docker compose build`), reading it in
# preference to any context-root `.dockerignore`. Patterns are evaluated against the build context
# (the repository root). The repo's `target/` alone is tens of GB, so excluding it here is what keeps
# the build context small. The Dockerfile also COPYs only the four workspace-member crates plus the
# root Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock, so anything excluded here is never needed.
target/
**/target/
.git/
build/
docs/
tools/
tmp/
test-config/
components/core/
components/webui/
components/clp-py-utils/
components/clp-package-utils/
components/job-orchestration/
components/clp-mcp-server/
components/package-template/
**/node_modules/
**/*.log
